    date: "2026-07-07",
    terms: "THE PROMOTION. By clicking on the \"Spin\" button (expression may vary) or entering the Promotion page, you agree to enroll as a member of the Promotion (\"Member\"). To unlock the Promotion, a Member should first place a qualifying order on the Promotion page. Once the Promotion is unlocked, a Member is entitled to collect a certain number of puzzle pieces and redeem the reward(s) on the Promotion page within the time limit.\n\nPuzzle pieces vary by color. The available methods for collecting each type of puzzle piece will be displayed on the Promotion page and may include: (i) completing daily check-in tasks; or (ii) placing qualifying orders on the Promotion page. The number of puzzle pieces a Member can collect per day is subject to a daily cap as displayed on the Promotion page.\n\nThe number and type of puzzle pieces required to redeem each reward are shown on the Promotion page. Rewards must be redeemed and claimed in sequence as displayed. Rewards include Temu Coupon(s), Temu Credit(s) and free gift(s) (collectively, \"Rewards\"). Please note that:\n\n(i) Temu Credit Reward(s) will be automatically credited to your account after you collect the required number of the corresponding puzzle pieces and redeem the corresponding Reward. The issuance of the Temu Credit Reward(s) will take a few days to proceed, but in no event longer than 90 days. Temu Credits will automatically be applied to the Member's future orders unless the Member decides not to use them. Temu Credits cannot be redeemed for cash.\n\n(ii) Temu Coupon Reward(s) will be automatically credited to the Member's account after the Member collects the required number of the corresponding puzzle pieces and redeem the corresponding Reward. Temu Coupons can be applied to the Member's future orders placed on Temu that meet the terms and conditions shown on the Temu Coupons to reduce the payment amount but cannot be used within this Promotion. Temu Coupons awarded in the Promotion will expire at 23:59 local time on the day after being claimed by the Member from the Promotion page. Each Temu Coupon can only be redeemed on a purchase that exceeds the indicated threshold (if any) or Temu's minimum order amount requirement (if applicable), whichever is higher.\n\n(iii) For free gift Reward(s), after collecting all required puzzle pieces, the Member must place an additional qualifying order on the Promotion page for each gift to claim it. Certain taxes and shipping fees may apply.\n\nEach order placed within this Promotion is subject to the minimum order amount requirement as displayed on the Promotion page. If a Member cancels or applies for a refund for any qualifying order, in whole or in part, the puzzle pieces collected by the Member with respect to such qualifying order will be taken back. If, as a result, the Member's total puzzle pieces become insufficient for any Reward that has already been redeemed, that Reward will be canceled and taken back. Additionally, if a Member cancels or applies for a refund for the additional qualifying order used to claim a free gift Reward, that free gift Reward will also be canceled and taken back.\n\nThe interface displayed on the Promotion page (if any) may simulate a \"wheel\", \"gift box\", \"cards\" or \"gold eggs\", the functions of which are for illustrative purposes only. This Promotion does not involve any form of chance, auctions, or contests and is based on objective criteria, i.e., everyone will get the best result in such functions.\n\nTIME LIMIT. The \"Time Limit\" for the Promotion will be displayed on the Promotion page.",
    pending: true,
    rules: [
      { t: "Seems like: Spend 50$ to get 50$ in credits. Requires an initial 10$, plus an extra 20$ for the missing blue pieces, plus a final 20$ to claim the 50$ credit." },
      { t: "The qualifying purchase uses the order amount before reductions, so a $0 purchase can qualify", warn: true },
      { t: "Bonus purchases use the final amount as the qualifying number, taxes included", warn: true },
    ],
    calc: {
      note: "How to calculate if you'll finish the promo:",
      formula: `p<sub>target</sub> − (p<sub>initial</sub> + p<sub>bonus</sub> + (d<sub>total</sub> − d<sub>missed</sub>) × r<sub>daily</sub>)`,
      rows: true,
      fields: [
        { k: "ib", label: "Initial blue", value: "5", row: "Initial", icon: "b", step: "1" },
        { k: "iy", label: "Initial yellow", value: "5", icon: "y", step: "1" },
        { k: "bb", label: "Bonus blue", value: "0", row: "Bonus", icon: "b", step: "1" },
        { k: "by", label: "Bonus yellow", value: "3", icon: "y", step: "1" },
        { k: "db", label: "Daily blue", value: "1", row: "Daily", icon: "b", step: "1" },
        { k: "dy", label: "Daily yellow", value: "2", icon: "y", step: "1" },
        { k: "d", label: "Total days", value: "20", row: "Days", tag: "total", step: "1" },
        { k: "md", label: "Days missed", value: "0", tag: "missed", step: "1" },
      ],
      out: "remaining",
      f: `(() => { const n = [ib, iy, bb, by, db, dy, d, md]; if (n.some(v => !isFinite(v))) return "—"; const dd = Math.max(0, d - md), b = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(27 - ib - bb - db * dd)), y = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(18 - iy - by - dy * dd)); if (y > 0) return "∞ (Impossible!)"; if (b) return b + " blue (" + Math.ceil(b / 6) + " additional 20$+ order(s))"; return "0! Make a final $20 purchase to get your credit!"; })()`,
    },
