    date: "2026-03-08",
    terms: "THE PROMOTION. By clicking on the \"Pick now\" (expression may vary) button on the Promotion page or registering and joining the Promotion, a user agrees to enroll as a member of the Promotion (a \"Member\"). The free products available through this Promotion are collectively referred to as \"Rewards\" (each, a \"Reward\"), which include: (1) Gifts (defined below) obtained through the Clover-Bar, and (2) Prizes (defined below).\n\nEarning Prizes via Crop Farming\n\nA Member may choose certain product(s) on the Promotion page (the \"Chosen Product(s)\") and is entitled to receive the Chosen Products for free (the \"Prize(s)\") if the Member successfully accumulates the designated value by farming and collecting the crops within the Time Limit (defined below). To farm the crops, Members need to collect water drop amounts by completing the tasks as indicated on the Promotion page and water the crops.\n\nAll unused water drop amounts will expire after the Time Limit ends. The quantity of available Water Drops is subject to a maximum threshold. If the number of Water Drops exceeds this threshold, certain excess Water Drops may only be collectible to the extent that redeemed Water Drops are actually used at the relevant time to free up available capacity. In such circumstances, Members may collect such Water Drops proportionally based on the redeemed Water Drops so used.\n\nNotwithstanding the foregoing, if the Member has successfully claimed the Prizes, the Member will not be able to further collect water drop amounts, but the unused water drop amounts will be carried over to the next round of the Promotion (if any).\n\nThe value a Member can get by farming the crops will decline within the range as displayed on the page. The maximum water drops needed to raise a crop are up to 100,000 units. The Promotion may also allow Members to earn water drops and/or other rewards through other in-Promotion games and/or tasks. The instructions and conditions are displayed on the Promotion page where applicable.\n\nEarning Gifts via the Clover-Bar\n\nMembers may also be entitled to receive a specified number of selected free item(s) (each, a \"Gift\") when Members complete the progress bar listed on the Promotion page (\"Clover-Bar\"). The combined value of all Gifts may be capped at a specified amount which will be listed on the Promotion page. To fill the Clover-Bar, Members are required to earn enough clover-points (\"Clovers\") by placing qualifying orders from the Promotion page (each, a \"Qualifying Order\") within the specified Time Limit.\n\nThe number of Clovers earned from each Qualifying Order is subject to a cap, which may vary by order and will be displayed on the Promotion page. The Qualifying Orders are subject to the minimum order threshold which will be listed on the Promotion page. Members can also earn water drops by placing Qualifying Orders within the Time Limit. The number of water drops earned from each order and other restrictions are subject to the separate \"Rules of Water Drops\".\n\nIf a Member, in whole or in part, cancels or applies for a refund for any Qualifying Order, the following shall apply: (1) if the corresponding Gift(s) have not yet been redeemed, all progress on the Progress Bar that was directly contributed by such order will be deducted; (2) if redemption of the corresponding Gift(s) has already occurred, it will be deemed forfeited.\n\nThe interface displayed on the Promotion page may simulate interactive functions such as \"jackpot\", \"wheel\", \"gift box\" or \"cards\" for illustrative purposes only. Everyone will get the best result in such interactive functions.\n\nTIME LIMIT. The \"Time Limit\" for the Promotion is as displayed on the Promotion page.",
    reward: "Water a virtual plant to 100% and get free items. Every single thing on the page wants you to buy something first",
